faq:
  - q: "What sports does RosterWise currently cover?"
    a: "RosterWise Soccer is available now, covering men's and women's NCAA D1, D2, D3, and NAIA programs. RosterWise Volleyball and RosterWise Lacrosse release this month — both covering men's and women's programs across NCAA D1, D2, D3, NAIA, and NJCAA. Softball, field hockey, and more are planned. Each sport launches as its own app."
  - q: "Is this a subscription?"
    a: "No. RosterWise is a one-time purchase of $40. No monthly fees, no annual renewals, no ads. You pay once and get lifetime access for your athlete's entire recruiting journey."
  - q: "What divisions does RosterWise cover?"
    a: "Soccer covers NCAA Division I, II, III, and NAIA. Volleyball and Lacrosse cover NCAA Division I, II, III, NAIA, and NJCAA — both men's and women's programs. Every program with a published roster is included."
  - q: "How current is the roster data?"
    a: "Roster data is refreshed regularly throughout the recruiting cycle. Each data refresh is captured from the official athletics website of every program, so the analysis reflects the current state of each roster."
  - q: "Will I get future updates?"
    a: "Yes. Lifetime access includes ongoing data refreshes for the sport you purchase. As rosters change each season, RosterWise updates the analysis automatically."
  - q: "What is My RosterFit™?"
    a: "My RosterFit™ is RosterWise's personalized scoring system. Enter your athlete's position, height, graduation year, GPA, test scores, and geographic preferences — and RosterFit scores every program based on how well your athlete's profile aligns with the program's actual roster composition. <a href='/roster-intelligence/'>Learn more about our roster intelligence methodology.</a>"
  - q: "Will RosterWise tell me which schools will recruit my athlete?"
    a: "No — and we're upfront about that. No tool can predict recruiting outcomes, because they depend on individual circumstances, coach communication, timing, and many factors no dataset can capture. What RosterWise does is give families the analysis to make better-informed decisions about where to focus their recruiting effort. It's intelligence, not a crystal ball."
  - q: "Do you offer recruiting consulting or coach outreach?"
    a: "No. RosterWise is a self-service intelligence tool, not a recruiting service. We focus on giving families the data and analysis to do their own research — because nobody knows your athlete's situation better than your family."
